  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, and it passes the typecheck. I haven't run `vite build` or looked at a rendered frame, because I have no shell or browser here.\n\n- **Star:** an emissive sphere at the centre, with a warm point light that lights the planets. A bloom effect gives it the glow.\n- **Planets:** five spheres with different sizes, colours, orbit radii (2.6 to 9.2) and speeds. They are repositioned every frame from `f.time`.\n- **Ring:** the fourth planet has a tilted, flattened torus ring that follows it around its orbit.\n- **Background and camera:** a near-black background, and a perspective camera at (0, 17, 16) looking at the origin. It should frame all orbits, but I haven't confirmed that in a rendered frame.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set to true one animation frame after the first `onFrame` callback. The engine's `createAuraApp` runs its own animation-frame loop, so I didn't add a separate `requestAnimationFrame` loop.\n- **Torus orientation:** I read the engine's torus geometry to set the ring's size and rotation. It is built in the XY plane and thin along Z. I rotate it by about π/2 about X to lay it flat, but I haven't checked the result visually.\n\n",
